  "reason": "Inspected all eight actual captures and FSB comparisons. All Tier-1 checks pass (IoU .9540/.9086/.9199, color delta 5.30/5.83/8.13), but visual review rejects. The sagittal hair cut was clipped to the narrow front face width, leaving lateral slabs. Renormalizing surviving views creates blue/teal islands where the side view is intermittently occluded. Long sparse tunic triangles are undersampled by equal chart allocation. Correct the SDF cut extent, retain absent per-view facing weights as explicit inferred continuation, and allocate atlas resolution from solved-camera pixel spans. No gate or source changes.",
